WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.360
On March 23, all of a sudden, the Russian president Vladimir Putin gave

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.520
orders to the Russian Central Bank and the Gazprom national

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.000
corporation to take on a new mechanism to levy Russian natural gas payments sold for "Unfriendly" countries

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
in ruble (the Russian national currency). Putin demanded, in his speech to the government

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.120
to exhaust the issue in just one week, which means that, by the 30th of March

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.480
all the ‘Unfriendly’ countries have to start paying in Russian ruble

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.000
Which countries are unfriendly? Countries that imposed

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.400
sanctions on Russia after Ukraine invasion on 24 February

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.560
the number of those countries goes up to 48 countries, Chief among which are the United States

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.120
European Union states, Britain, Japan, Canada, Norway

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.480
Singapore, South Korea, Switzerland and Ukraine itself

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.200
The decision is the first by Russia considering the use of natural

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.200
gas supplies as a weapon in the ongoing conflict between it and the West regarding the war in Ukraine

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:25.280
It came at a time wherein the Russian economy is facing the most serious crisis in years (since the dissolution of the Soviet Union)

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.880
it also deepens the confrontation with Western world and could exacerbate the worst energy crisis in Europe, since the 1970s

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:36.360
due to its heavy dependence on Russian gas for heating and power generation

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:42.360
That is why the prices of natural gas in Europe rose by 30% after this decision

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.800
Putin's clear message was: You want our gas, You need our currency

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.920
On this subject, we ask a few questions: What is the rejoinder of countries that are not friendly

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.280
to Russia regarding a decision like this? Do they really pay in rubles?

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.680
Were the contracts between Russia and these countries originally paid in rubles?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.640
Why does Russia want them to pay in rubles for gas?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.040
Will this affect the highly dominated US dollar all over the world?

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.920
What would be the other possible options if those countries refrained from payment in Ruble?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.480
All these questions and more are going to be answered in today's episode

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.800
I am Ashraf Ibrahim and this is the Economic Informant

