00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.760
Russia is the richest country in the world with gas

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.680
it has a total of 47 trillion cubic meters of natural gas reserves

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.840
It is also the largest exporter of natural gas all over the world

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.400
About 196 billion cubic meters are shipped annually from

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.160
Russia to different countries all over the world, so to speak

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.400
Our main concerns in today's episode are; Russia's exports of

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.760
natural gas to Europe, which is Russia's largest gas importer over the past decades

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.320
Gazprom, a national corporation owned by the Russian government

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.200
is in control of everything related to natural gas in Russia

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.640
including natural gas supplies to other countries

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.120
It supplies Europeans with 40% of their needs of natural gas

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.680
Most of those 40% pass through pipelines as follows

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.800
The first network of pipelines are transport corridors across Ukraine

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.280
It includes the Brotherhood pipeline, which is the oldest in the region

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:41.880
It was constructed in 1967 from Russia through Ukraine to end in Slovakia

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:47.360
In 1984, the Urengoy - Pomary - Uzhgorod line was adopted

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.040
which is in fact Not just one line, but a stream of gas lines

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.000
connected together and extending from the Urengoy gas field in

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.240
Siberia to the city of Uzhhorod in the far west of Ukraine

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.960
and from there to Slovakia. After 4 years of that one

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.120
the ‘Progress line’ was constructed and it extended from the

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:12.280
Yamburg gas field in northern Russia; following the same route of the Urengoy–Pomary–Uzhgorod pipeline to Slovakia

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.680
As you can see, all these lines go far to Slovakia

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.480
From Slovakia, there are two branches: one goes to the Czech Republic

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.000
and from there it reaches the municipality of Weidhaus in

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.000
Bavaria on the Czech-German border

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.000
The other one goes from Slovakia to Austria

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.640
and from Austria to Italy and Slovenia

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.040
All these countries depend on Russian gas.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.760
There is a fourth gas pipeline that passes through Ukraine

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.200
the So yuz gas pipeline, which was built in 1980 and extends

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.000
from Orenburg in southwestern Russia all through Ukrainian

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.240
lands passing by Hungary

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.000
to deliver gas to Slovakia and Romania as well

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.240
Still in Ukraine as well, there is a transit gas pipeline built in 1986

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.040
and it passes through the Ukrainian and Romanian

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.000
lands delivering gas to Bulgaria

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.640
Turkey, Greece and North Macedonia

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.520
This is the group of gas pipelines that pass through Ukraine and

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:11.560
transport 41.6 billion cubic meters of gas to Europe in 2021

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:15.240
The second main pipeline that connects Russia to Europe is

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:19.840
Nord Stream 1 which runs under the Baltic Sea from Portovaya

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.160
Bay near the city of Vyborg in western Russia

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.000
to the German coast near Greifswald

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.400
with a length of 1,224 km

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.120
This giant pipeline was built in 2011

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.920
and it delivers almost 55 billion cubic meters of gas

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.000
from which Germany, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.720
France, Denmark and other European countries benefit

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:45.800
The third main pipeline that delivers Russian gas to Europe is Yamal-Europe

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.720
It is a long pipeline that collects gas from natural gas fields

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:53.960
in the Yamal Peninsula and Western Siberia and goes through

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.680
Belarusian lands, then Polish lands to Germany

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.880
with a length of 4107 km

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.240
It was constructed in 1996

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.360
with a full capacity of 33 billion cubic meters of natural gas

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.760
These were the pipelines that transported Russian natural gas

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.360
to European countries and which transported most of the

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.600
quantities that Russia exported to Europe as a whole

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:20.560
Over the past year, 2021, Russia exported 155 billion cubic

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.480
meters of gas to Europe through this pipeline network

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:28.360
Nevertheless, these countries whose economic life depends strategically on the Russian natural gas that flows in these pipelines

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:33.200
are suddenly obliged to pay in rubles, otherwise, the natural gas pumps may be turned off

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:39.000
Well, the question that pops up here is: How much do Russian gas exports cost in the first place? What currency were the former financial transactions in?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.880
Attention please!

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.600
According to the Central Bank of Russia

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:48.280
Russia's total exports in 2021 went up to $489.8 billion

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:54.680
Gas and LNG pipelines made $61.8 billion

00:06:54.680 --> 00:07:00.240
So to speak, about 12.6% of the total exports come from gas

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:01.600
Furthermore, the countries hostile to Russia,

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.800
which the latter demands to pay in rubles 

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:07.560
account for almost 70% of Russian gas exports

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.160
What was the currency in which these countries used to pay in?

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.360
According to Gazprom, natural gas sales to Europe

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.240
and other countries were settled as follows

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:21.320
58% of sales were in euros, 39% were in dollars

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.920
and about 3% were in sterling

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.600
Naturally, the euro is the most paid currency in gas sales

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.960
because Europe is Russia's largest client

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:35.240
This takes us to the situation of these countries regarding the Russian decision to pay in rubles

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:40.640
The European community in particular, once they knew, told Putin that it is impossible to pay in rule and he must stop joking!

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.560
European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:49.400
said that this step is just an attempt to circumvent EU sanctions against Russia

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:57.000
She said: “We will not allow our sanctions to be circumvented. The time when energy could be used to blackmail us is over.”

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:03.080
The German Economy Minister said that Putin's demand for payment in rubles is “a unilateral and clear breach of existing contracts”

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:08.360
The Minister of Finance advised German energy suppliers not to pay for Russian gas in rubles

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:14.520
and said: “We cannot accept Putin’s terms, but stick to the contracts as they were concluded.”

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:21.520
The CEO of PGNiG, the largest Polish energy company, which contracted with Gazprom

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:30.400
said simply that the company will not pay in rubles, adding that the other partner in the contract - Gazprom - can not change the method of payment in such a way

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.160
The same is Italy which announced that payment will be in euros as used to

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:40.600
The United States has no part in this matter of course as it imposed an immediate ban on Russian oil and gas imports

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:47.760
The United Kingdom said it will gradually ban gas imports by the end of the year 2022

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.000
Apart from Europe and the United States, which are at the center of the confrontation with Russia

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.800
It is noticed that the reaction of Asian customers was pretty softer

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:00.400
Japan, which is the largest importer of Russian liquefied natural gas in Asia

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.760
said that it is studying the implications regarding payment in rubles

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:08.040
South Korea, which is the third largest importer of liquefied natural gas in Asia

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:12.600
said that it would do anything to continue importing Russian gas

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:15.720
which clearly means that they have no problem paying in rubles

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:20.320
So, what is expected to happen if European countries refuse to pay in rubles?

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.840
Most likely, the catastrophe that the whole world has been afraid of

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.000
since the beginning of the Russian war on Ukraine will happen

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.480
There will be no more Russian gas for Europe 

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.760
What happened hours before the filming of this episode on Monday, March 28

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.080
says that the situation is just heading this way

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.480
As the presidency of the Group of Seven recently took place

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.600
the ministers of the industrialized countries rejected Russia's demands to pay in rubles

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.880
At the same time, Russia said that it would not provide Europe

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:47.200
with gas for free because it offered mechanisms for paying in

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.400
rubles and it is them who refused

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:52.280
Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said sarcastically that in our

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:57.000
current situation we cannot participate in charitable works

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.600
meaning that they can not provide gas to European customers for free

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:04.040
He said that Russia will take decisions in due course if European

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.000
states refuse to pay in the Russian currency

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.880
Putin’s decision put the Europeans in a real dilemma, so to speak

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:14.200
If they refuse to pay in rubles, insisting that Russia is committing a unilateral violation of contracts

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.160
the gas pumping will be turned off

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:22.880
If they do pay in rubles, they will be  supporting the Russian ruble, thus easing the sanctions imposed on Russia

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:28.200
This last point highlights a logical question: why does Russia want gas payments to be in ruble?

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:32.200
Isn't it supposed that the country needs hard currency like the euro and dollar?

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.120
It is not always the case, everything has a time and place

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:37.360
Payment in rubles, if it happens, will lead to an increase in demand for

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.080
it by gas customers in the list of unfriendly countries previously clarified

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:44.920
This will consequently lead to an increase in its value against other major currencies

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:47.480
Repercussions actually took place since the decision was made

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.120
The ruble went from depreciating to stabilizing

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:55.360
At the time of writing this episode, the exchange value is $1 for 99 ruble

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:01.120
Although it is 17% weaker than its normal levels before the Russian invasion of Ukraine

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:07.600
it is stronger than it was on March 7 when it reached its lowest level which was 151 rubles per dollar

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:11.800
Moreover, it is expected that its value will rise up even more if the importing countries agree to pay in ruble

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:17.360
Secondly, this will force customers, especially Europeans, to buy rubles

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:22.600
from Russian banks that are subject to sanctions, and this means that sanctions will be eased

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:27.160
Third, the sanctions created an unprecedented economic isolation for Russia

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.800
which is not even able to use the surplus dollars or euros

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:34.920
It is merely like imprisoning someone with one million dollars in a room

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:38.000
They would starve to death though being surrounded by money

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:42.080
Russia has a surplus in the current account, which includes the trade surplus

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:45.320
meaning that the value of its exports is more than the value of its imports

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:50.640
In 2021, it achieved a surplus of 120.3 billion dollars

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.280
Fourthly, despite the aforementioned points, the dollar and the euro will settle in Russia in the end

00:11:56.280 --> 00:12:00.800
as the Western companies will buy the ruble and sell the dollar and the euro to Russian banks

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:05.840
So, a demand for the ruble, that did not exist before, is being created

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:10.720
The fifth and most important thing is that the pricing and settlement of global commodities such as oil and gas

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:18.960
in major currencies, specifically the dollar and the euro, will strengthen their position and prove their dominance over international trade

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.840
That is why 80% of global reserves are in dollars and euros

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:28.440
Surely Russia will bend all backwards to shake this hegemony

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:34.120
This drives us to a significant question: Will Russia's pay in ruble decision

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:37.000
affect the dollar's dominance over the global economy?

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:42.800
This step can be considered an extension of Russia’s attempt to remove the dollar from its economy;

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:48.160
an attempt it started with China since Western countries imposed sanctions on Russia

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.600
after its annexation of the Crimea peninsula in 2014

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:57.560
For example, Russia replaced the dollar with the euro or local currencies in trade between Russia, China and India,

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:02.000
reducing the Russian Central Bank’s holdings of US dollar reserves,

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.400
and excluding dollar assets from the sovereign wealth fund.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:09.280
All these were attempts to influence the dollar’s hegemony in the world,

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:12.200
and the move to pay in rubles is just a new step in the way.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:17.360
However, Considering what things have come to, it is crystal clear that Putin’s decision had a small effect

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:28.520
On the contrary, the US dollar index USDX, which measures the value of the dollar against the most important six other major currencies

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:32.040
namely the euro, the Japanese yen, the British pound

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.720
the Canadian dollar, the Swedish krona and the Swiss franc,

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.520
shows a rise in the value of the dollar against all these other major currencies

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:45.760
from the beginning of 2022 until the time of writing this episode by 3%.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:51.480
In short, the pay in ruble decision will have a very limited impact on the dominance of the dollar

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:57.800
In short, Russia is adamant in the pay in ruble decision and will not back down one iota.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:01.400
The countries that it describes as hostile / unfriendly must acquiesce in this.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:08.760
On the other hand, European countries will be most affected by this issue, as they are adamant not to pay in ruble.

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:12.600
So, what is going to happen is subjected to several scenarios, we will not address them all,

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.480
but the most important three of them, and they are as follows:

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:19.560
The first scenario is that the deadline, that still has two days from the time of filming this episode,

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:25.320
ends and each party adheres to its position, so, Russia starts cutting off the gas pipelines to Europe

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:31.000
for the first time since the seventies when the Soviet Union began building these gas pipelines.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:36.160
Here the Europeans will be subjected to a drastic crisis that their continent has not witnessed in decades,

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:41.360
a crisis as a result of which factories will stop running, houses electricity will be cut off,

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:47.840
natural gas prices will rise terribly, and a major state of paralysis and economic confusion will occur

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:53.640
The second scenario is that some European countries agree to pay in rubles, as the deadline Putin has put is approaching,

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:58.760
while others refuse, risking Russia might have to cut off gas to their countries.

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:03.280
At that time, these countries will try to compensate for the shortage of Russian gas from other sources

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:06.280
such as liquefied natural gas from the United States and Qatar

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:12.800
However, this will raise Natural gas prices all across Europe too, but not as high as expected at the previous scenario

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:18.240
The third scenario is that all European countries refuse to pay in rubles

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:22.840
and here instead of cutting off energy supplies to all of Europe;

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:25.960
Russia will be satisfied with operating one or two main pipelines,

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:31.920
consequently a major energy crisis will break out all over the continent pushing gas prices to rise highly,

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.880
this consequently will put pressure on European governments

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.520
to the extent that they would settle an agreement anyway.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:41.360
Here, Russia does not take the option of Samson bringing down the columns and collapsing the temple over everyone's,

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.480
in contrast it leaves an empty room to accord on a common ground.

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:48.240
This is a scenario that we can consider as a pinch from Russia in order to force European countries

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:50.960
to agree upon terms that will lead to the Russians real gains.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:55.760
In your opinion, which of all these scenarios is the most likely to happen?

00:15:55.760 --> 00:16:01.200
Is it possible to see a pure fourth scenario in the coming days? I will follow up all your answers in the comments.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.920
In the end, like and share and subscribe to the channel if you like the episode,

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:12.160
tell your friends about the channel, they may like it too, Goodbye.

